    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on August 21, 2026, **Corbin Carroll** leads the way as our strongest start with an elite 78.75 score. While he faces a left-handed arm in Nick Lodolo, the park factors and his intrinsic ability to produce against high-skill pitching keep his ceiling significantly higher than the rest of the roster. **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Isaac Paredes** also project as high-floor anchors today, both benefiting from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.00 and strong lineup placement that positions them to maximize RBI opportunities. The decision to prioritize **Mickey Moniak** despite a challenging platoon split is driven largely by a massive +14% park advantage, pushing him to a 59.91 efficiency score that keeps him just ahead of our lower-tier utility options.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Josh Naylor** (58.40) narrowly edged out **Cole Young** (47.73). While **Cole Young** is a valuable asset in our SB-starved landscape, the optimizer favored **Josh Naylor** due to the raw projection gap and a favorable matchup against Matthew Boyd, whose 4.38 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for extra-base production. We are holding **Brice Turang** and **Austin Riley** on the bench today, as both draw elite, high-strikeout starters\u2014Chris Sale and Jeferson Misiorowski, respectively\u2014which suppressed their efficiency scores well below the threshold for active duty.\n\nManagers should note that all projected scores currently rely on assumed lineup positions. We are monitoring statuses closely, as any deviation in the batting order for **Gabriel Moreno** or **Henry Bolte** could impact their favorable projections, specifically the +10% order bonus assigned to **Henry Bolte** in the leadoff spot. With most of our starters facing pitchers sporting xERAs near or above 4.00, today offers a high-upside environment for our core hitters to capitalize on volume, provided the weather holds and our projected lineup spots remain accurate.",
